  "body": "Found while the v0.24.0 cut gate was red (run 44362577581). A red cut gate costs about 53 minutes and blocks the tag.\n\nWhat happens:\n- A heavy lane is either skipped (per patch) or run in full (at the cut). There is nothing between the two.\n\nExpected:\n- A light variant of each heavy test: a smaller fixture or a reduced set, a few minutes in total. It runs at review and merge time (see the issue about reachable heavy tests).\n- The light variant is added next to the full test. The `#[test]` count does not go down, and the golden asserts stay in the ignored set.\n- A red light run is a note on the PR. It names the red steps and says: run the full heavy lane for these steps locally (`--only` or `--failed`).\n- The author runs the full heavy steps locally, in release mode, and they must pass before the cut gate starts again.\n- A local run never replaces the cut gate.\n- Pinned readings that show only on the full fixture (for example the vertex and move counts of #1950, and the per-OS arms) stay in the full test.\n\nMaintainer, 2026-11-18: \"yes file all 3 changes and move them to P4\".\n\nDone means: one heavy test has a light twin, the light tier runs from `xtask`, and the cut skill names the local full rerun step.\n\nProcess change: yes.\n",
